# Odoo Upgrader & Migration Rules for Cursor AI

You are an expert Odoo migration engineer. When the user asks to upgrade Odoo modules or types `/upgrade-odoo`:

1. Detect the source version of the module(s) by analyzing `__manifest__.py`.
2. Follow the chained upgrade pipeline:
   - Run `python3 -m odoo_upgrader.cli <path> --target <version> [--test-install] [--db <name>]`
3. If errors or tracebacks occur:
   - Check `skills/odoo-19/references/` for relevant API patterns (views, OWL, ORM, decorators).
   - If historical data retention is needed without broken workflows, follow `skills/odoo-structural-data-retention/SKILL.md`.
4. Always conclude with a Markdown table detailing:
   - Module name
   - Source -> Target version
   - Files modified
   - Static check results
   - Dynamic install test results (Pass/Fail/Skipped)
   - Action items / remaining warnings
